{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "An order of the Knights Radiant whose Surges are Progression and Illumination.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "52" }]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Truthwatchers use Progression, the Surge of growth and healing, and Illumination, which crafts illusions by weaving light and sound.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Renarin says Truthwatchers are special because \"they see\".",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "89" }]
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The Ancient Radiants",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "52" }]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "An old account calls the Truthwatchers esoteric: none of them spoke or wrote of what they did, and their silence came from tact rather than disdain.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "52" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The True Desolation",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "89" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "116" },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "54" },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "114" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Renarin swears to be a Truthwatcher.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "89" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jasnah and her spren discover that Renarin's spren, Glys, is corrupted, yet somehow bonded to a human.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "116" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Renarin sees visions of what may come. He tells Dalinar that he and Odium both see only possible outcomes, and that their powers interfere with each other.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "54" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Rlain bonds a corrupted mistspren, Tumi, and becomes a Truthwatcher.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "114" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Ideals of the Truthwatchers",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "The Ideals of the Knights Radiant, also called the Immortal Words, are rules the Radiants live by. The First Ideal is shared by every order; each order then has four more of its own.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "59" }]
        }
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "The First Ideal",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "59" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Truthwatchers share the First Ideal with every other order; it serves as the motto of the Knights Radiant.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "59" }]
            }
          ],
          "words": [
            {
              "text": "Life before death, strength before weakness, journey before destination.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "59" }],
              "spokenBy": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Abilities",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Truthwatchers use the Surges of Progression and Illumination.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }]
        }
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Progression",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" },
                    { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "50" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Progression, the Surge of growth and healing, alters how living things grow and heal.",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "It heals harm to a person's body and soul at once and without scars, though harder healings take skill.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" },
                    { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "50" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Illumination",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "6" },
                { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "141" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Illumination crafts illusions by weaving light and sound.",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "prologue" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Truthwatchers use it for disguises, for illusory walls and rocks to hide in, and to confuse or distract.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "6" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "The Truthwatcher Honorbearer summons a globe of light that brings shadows to life, speaking with the voices of the people Szeth has killed.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "141" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Corrupted spren",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "116" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "120" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "6" },
                { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "84" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Enlightened",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "84" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Renarin's spren, Glys, is corrupted, yet bonded to a human.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "116" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "With a corrupted spren, Progression still works as usual: Renarin heals Adolin with Stormlight. By drawing in a great deal of Stormlight, he also makes a wounded thunderclast's spirit flee its body.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "120" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Instead of illusions, Renarin can only summon lights, which sometimes act strangely.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "6" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Inside the Spiritual Realm, Enlightened Truthwatchers can exert some control over it. They can also hear Odium's rhythms.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "84" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Future sight",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "118" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "54" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "i-6" },
                { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "30" },
                { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "84" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Renarin sees visions of possible futures, shown in stained glass. They are not always accurate: a vision about Jasnah does not come true.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "118" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "The visions don't come from Odium, though Odium may influence what they show.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "54" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Odium cannot see the future of Renarin and those close to him: it shows as a blacked-out place.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "i-6" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Rlain can enter one of Renarin's visions with him. The visions come when the rhythms of Roshar swell.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "30" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Ba-Ado-Mishram can affect the visions in small ways.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "84" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Sphere light",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "8" },
                { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "62" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Renarin can summon a light that shows an illusion of a person's other self.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "8" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "The light can show a person an alternate version of themselves, and it responds better when given a Command.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "62" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Nahel bond abilities",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "63" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "With a strong enough bond, an Enlightened Truthwatcher and their mistspren can feel each other's emotions.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "63" }]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
